error: `greet` holds the thread until it is done, and an async function does not hold its thread
  the tasks of async functions share a few threads: one that holds its thread keeps the others from running
  --> error_async_blocking_call.sg:12:11
 12 |     print(greet())
    |           ^^^^^
  `greet` calls `ask`, which does `Stdin.readLine` here:
  --> error_async_blocking_call.sg:3:15
 3 |     _ = Stdin.readLine(ref line)
   |               ^^^^^^^^
  hint: a function that does it runs on a thread of its own with `await Task.run(work, x)`
